The Integration Architect (Systems & Data Flow)
* MCP Dual-Transport Interface Cohesion: In Project 1 of the roadmap, supporting both stdio IPC and HTTP with Server-Sent Events (SSE) ensures the Crabdeck Megabrain can communicate with external tools either via fast local process pipes or network-agnostic streaming streams. However, schema synchronization between Pydantic models in Python and Zod schemas in TypeScript requires an automated code generation step (e.g., json-schema-to-typescript) during CI to prevent contract drift across tool definitions.
* Optical Ray-Tracing Ray Cache in ClayPraxinoscopeEngine: In main.js, the Optical Ray-Tracing view calculates reflection angles from 12 polygon mirror facets per frame. Since the geometry of a regular dodecagon is fixed, the mirror face normals and vertex positions relative to the central spindle should be precomputed into a static lookup table, computing only the global rotational matrix per frame to optimize 60 FPS rendering.
The Permissions Guard / Red Teamer (Security, Privacy & Blast Radius)
* Multi-Platform Kernel Process Confinement: Project 2 correctly identifies Win32 Job Objects (on Windows 11 host workstations) and POSIX rlimits (on Linux/Termux) as the true security perimeter. Soft Python wrappers or try/except blocks are insufficient when executing untrusted agent-generated code. Enforcing hard limits on job memory, restricting token access, and disallowing child process creation at the OS level ensures runaway agent loops cannot exhaust host memory or spawn orphaned daemons.
* Nonce Replay Vulnerability: The HMAC-SHA256 approval nonce must include a monotonic counter or microsecond timestamp with a strict expiration window (e.g., 300 seconds) to prevent replay attacks if approval tokens are leaked or intercepted over local telemetry logs.
